{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 107, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free skip with a 3x3 conv on the input edge gives a huge gain (+43/+45/+17), far larger than replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip on the output edge to a 3x3 conv gives +45/+46/+17.5, far more than from 1x1 or avg_pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing skip with a 3x3 conv on the direct edge gives large gains, versus small or negative changes when replacing avg_pool, none or 1x1."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a skip for a 3x3 conv on edge 2 gives about +35/+32/+11, while other parents see roughly zero change."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing skip with a 1x1 conv on edge 1 gives clear gains on all datasets, whereas replacing 3x3 or avg_pool gives zero or negative change."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on the input edge hurts strongly (-1.5 to -11.6) versus roughly neutral when removing a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on edge 2 costs several points (-3.4/-6.4/-11.6), unlike removing weaker ops that is near neutral."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling on the output edge consistently loses accuracy, more than when replacing a 1x1 conv."